WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.380
A line stretches across the
screen: your whole life.

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.580
Then it starts to shrink.

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:12.310
Years vanish, then days, then hours,
until one bright tick is left,

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.980
and the clock stops.

5
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.360
A lover asks: "Out of your
whole life give but a moment!"

6
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.370
One moment, against a whole lifetime.

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.290
Can it really matter more?

8
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.780
In this mission, you'll find out
what that moment would prove:

9
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.610
"This tick of our life-time's
one moment you love me!"

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.570
You'll feel the poem's
rush: fourteen lines,

11
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.750
like a sonnet, but breathless.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.850
And you'll puzzle over a
phrase that sounds impossible:

13
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.790
"The moment eternal".

14
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.580
Your mission: decide whether one moment
can matter more than a whole life.
